      "text": "Flight to Santiago and city tour"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "1d113b414850c8fc6415026ed184716ab1ab660b99a3c11f081ab743ef824e33",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw9pzpme-g1f7fnp0wz",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to Mendoza Airport and fly to Santiago.\n\nOn arrival, you will be met and transferred to your hotel.\n\nAfter checking in and taking some time to rest, set out on a sightseeing tour of the Chilean capital.\n\nSantiago lies in a valley surrounded by mountains. Colonial buildings that have survived numerous earthquakes still stand in the historic centre, while modern districts lie farther out.\n\nYour first stop is San Cristóbal Hill and Santiago Metropolitan Park. Here you can take a walk, visit the zoo and see the statue of the Virgin Mary.\n\nThe tour continues in the historic centre. You’ll see the Governor’s House, the Central Post Office, La Moneda Palace, Plaza de Armas and the Metropolitan Cathedral.\n\nThe square is also home to an opera and ballet theatre that has hosted renowned performers.\n\nThe tour ends in the modern districts of Santiago, with their hotels, bars, restaurants and shopping centres.\n\nReturn to the hotel."
    },
